PASS units mod 9: generators = units that are neither squares {1,4,7} nor cubes {1,8}; 2 is one (so 2 generates every (Z/3^k)^x)
PASS odd primes a < 400: 2 is a primitive root mod a^2 iff 2 lies in no q-th power clock mod a^2, q | a(a-1) prime
   (a, 2 primitive mod a^2, power clocks containing 2): [(3, True, []), (5, True, []), (7, False, [2]), (11, True, []), (13, True, []), (17, False, [2]), (19, True, []), (23, False, [2]), (29, True, []), (31, False, [2, 3]), (37, True, [])]
